# Project 01 - Single Multiply-Accumulate (MAC)

## Overview

This project implements a simple Multiply-Accumulate (MAC) unit in Verilog.

A MAC unit performs one of the most fundamental arithmetic operations in digital hardware:

Result = (A × B) + Accumulator

MAC units are widely used in:

- Digital Signal Processing (DSP)
- Finite Impulse Response (FIR) Filters
- Fast Fourier Transform (FFT)
- Matrix Multiplication
- Artificial Intelligence (AI)
- Machine Learning Accelerators
- CNN and DNN Hardware
- FPGA DSP48 Blocks

This project is the first step toward building larger hardware accelerators such as matrix multipliers, convolution engines, and systolic arrays.

---

## Architecture

```
         A
         │
         │
         ▼
      Multiplier
         │
         ▼
     Product (A×B)
         │
         ▼
       Adder
         ▲
         │
Accumulator Register
         │
         ▼
      MAC Output
```

